  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    This guide supports shoppers on the <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> directory at kakobuy-cn.com. Domestic tracking literacy used to map cleanly: Taobao rows implied Cainiao-flavoured scans; JD carts lived inside JD&apos;s mesh.
    Reporting around <strong>Double 11 2024</strong> documented a thaw—JD Logistics integrating with Taobao/Tmall merchants and Cainiao reciprocally supporting JD third-party sellers—which means spreadsheet curators must annotate <strong>carrier identity</strong> instead of assuming mall branding predicts routing.
  </p>

  <h2>What TechNode chronicled in autumn 2024</h2>
  <p>
    In <a href="https://technode.com/2024/11/05/undercurrents-in-double-11-whats-changed-and-whats-not/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechNode&apos;s November 2024 Double 11 analysis</a>, journalists noted Taobao and JD kicking off overlapping presale windows (Taobao/Tmall from <strong>14 October</strong>; JD-aligned beats from similar October cadences).
    More importantly for parcel archaeology: on <strong>16 October 2024</strong>, JD Logistics publicly partnered with Taobao Group so merchants could select JD warehousing and courier products; by <strong>28 October</strong>, Cainiao integrations reportedly opened Cainiao Express options to JD third-party merchants—consumers could therefore observe JD-branded legs inside Taobao apps.
  </p>

  <h2>Why Kakobuy Spreadsheet rows need a “carrier observed” field</h2>
  <p>
    Agent dashboards collapse messy mainland hops into buyer-legible statuses.
    When spreadsheets still embed assumptions like “Taobao == Cainiao-only,” moderators mis-diagnose stalled pickups.
    Add a lightweight column for <strong>domestic carrier + MAWB/handover hints</strong> once buyers paste logistics snippets—this complements URL hygiene guidance in <a href="/blog/kakobuy-links-discovery-url-hygiene/">links discovery essay</a>, not duplicate it.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits &amp; freshness</h2>
  <p>
    Partnership rhetoric evolves quarterly; use this piece as a <strong>historical anchor</strong> explaining why 2024–2026 tracking screenshots look hybridised.
    Strategic commentary does not override Kakobuy&apos;s warehouse timestamps—those remain canonical for QC triggers outlined in <a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-qc/">Spreadsheet QC essay</a>.
  </p>
</BlogArticleShell>
